# oracle: a fix colvars metadynamics state read back (colvarbias_meta::read_state_data): three biases (a 20-bin grid; an
#   expanding grid with keepHills; no grids on a vector colvar) run 40 steps, then unfix and a new fix colvars with
#   input ms1 continues for 30. The grids replace the configured ones with the parameters in the state (the expanded
#   boundaries), the kept hills are read as explicit hills, and hills not newer than the state's step are skipped
#   otherwise. Measured with native LAMMPS: "successfully read 8 explicit hills" for grow and 0 for nogrid (its hills
#   are all older than step 40, so the no-grid bias restarts empty); files within 1 ulp of the engine's (LJ bits).
# oracle-inputs: w775cv_metastate.colvars
# oracle-files: ms1.colvars.state ms2.colvars.traj ms2.colvars.state ms2.grid.pmf ms2.grow.pmf
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 filerel=1e-10
units           lj
atom_modify     map array
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
set             atom 1*128 type 2
mass            1 1.0
mass            2 2.5
velocity        all create 1.5 87287 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all colvars w775cv_metastate.colvars output ms1
fix_modify      2 energy yes
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal f_2 f_2[1][1] f_2[2][1]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             40
unfix           2
fix             2 all colvars w775cv_metastate.colvars input ms1 output ms2
fix_modify      2 energy yes
run             30
